{
  "title": "Olympic Peninsula",
  "indexDescription": "Olympic peninsula trip in July 2026.",
  "description": "July 2026 we toured the Olympic Peninsula for a few days driving our electric Kia.  \n\nThe first night we had dinner Grannies restaurant and spent the night in the hotel there.  We walked around Lake Crescent and walked to Marymere Falls.  We drove into the Olympic park and hiked to Sol duc falls.  \n\nAfter that we drove highway 101 to Forks where we spent two nights.  There was an empty 9 stall Rivian electric charging station we could use.  From Forks we took side trips the Hoh Rain Forest,  Rialto and Ruby beaches.  Then we drove down the coast for lunch and a walk on the beach at Kalaloch. and we continued to Lake Quinault were we spent the night at the lodge and hiked trials starting across the street.",
