    {
      "description": "Beach combing museum just outside of Forks. \n\nThis was an amazing place. We talked to the owner.  He is responsible for the finding all the stuff and running the  museum. He has been beach combing for 40 years. \n\nThe museum is in his big two story garage at his house. He had bins filled with the same kind of item, floats of every kind, boots, dolls, and weird stuff. He has a section for items found after the Japanese tsunami and he checke they're not radioactive.\n\nThe bigger stuff is outside in the yard. There were several row boats and a Hobie cat.",
